## STANDING LINES
1. **PRIOR-WORK CHECK** (step 2). No production, demo, UAT or hosted site; no `az`, docker, ssh; one fetch, one push, `gh -X GET`. **No message to any human**; no PR action; **no Jira write** (the records rows are the records seat's, not yours). Never skip a failure: fix the root cause and re-verify end to end. **Never delete** (`rm`, `branch -d`, `--prune`, `gc`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`, `checkout -- <file>`, `sed -i`): quarantine to `.tools/b1311/_quarantine/`. **This phase builds no integration with HP tools (Security Manager API, Fleet Threat Assessment, firmware tools, SIEM). Next-phase items are stored and architected only, never built, and never shown to HP as done.**
2. Shell: no `cd`; absolute single-quoted paths (`!`); `git -C`; `git --no-optional-locks` for reads; `${S}:path` with braces in zsh; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a control per count; `python3 -I -B`; a separator in `echo` is never a bare `====`. **Every count, `file:line` and clock is printed by a program.**
3. **Locks, load, heartbeats.** `.tools/.git-lock` (via `lock.sh`) wraps the fetch and push only. Heavy jobs (the whole `npm test`, lint, typecheck, build) through `hv.sh`, `df -k` first; a heartbeat that MOVES every 30 s into `.tools/b1311/logs/heartbeat.txt`. A heavy-slot wait is not a finding.
